; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk
; Expected: 15
; PROOF LEVEL: FKWU-STAGED / FOURTH-ARM ONLY (host_spawn, host_alive, host_wait and the kernel roster)
;
; zombie-alive-band — a process that has ended is not alive, whether or not its parent has waited.
;
; kill(pid, 0) succeeds for a zombie: a child that has exited and has not been reaped. host_alive, the
; roster's sweep and kernel_live_pids all asked kill alone, so on 2026-09-11 the ear organ's live lane —
; which ends at birth when no Metal carrier sits beside the binary — stayed "alive" to the ear for its whole
; birth patience, and to the roster, which kept its slot. libproc cannot tell: proc_pidinfo answers ESRCH
; for a zombie. The seed asks the process table (sysctl KERN_PROC_PID on macOS, /proc on Linux). Here a
; child ends and is deliberately not waited for, so it is a zombie when the question comes.
;
; Verdict 15:
;   1  the child spawns (a pid above zero) and is alive while it rests
;   2  after it has ended and before anyone waits, host_alive answers 0 — not 1
;   4  host_wait still reaps it and hands back its exit status, 0
;   8  once reaped, host_alive answers 0 and kernel_live_pids does not name it
(do
    (let child (host_spawn_quiet (list "./fkwu" "observe/tests/roster-sleeper.fk")))
    (let early (host_sleep_ms 700))
    (let alive-resting (host_alive child))
    (let late (host_sleep_ms 3500))
    (let alive-ended (host_alive child))
    (let status (host_wait child))
    (let alive-reaped (host_alive child))
    (let live (kernel_live_pids))
    (defn zab-in? (x xs) (if (eq (len xs) 0) 0 (if (eq (head xs) x) 1 (zab-in? x (tail xs)))))

    (let told (print (list "child" child "alive-resting" alive-resting "alive-ended-unreaped" alive-ended "status" status "alive-reaped" alive-reaped)))
    (let c0 (if (and (gt child 0) (eq alive-resting 1)) 1 0))
    (let c1 (if (eq alive-ended 0) 2 0))
    (let c2 (if (eq status 0) 4 0))
    (let c3 (if (and (eq alive-reaped 0) (eq (zab-in? child live) 0)) 8 0))
    (add c0 (add c1 (add c2 c3))))
